(Mind, I was responding to Jistan Idiot's question, not to your lost
game.)

But if that's what you restrict your choices to, then one answer is:
you cannot "defend" yourself against polytraps on the level if you
don't even detect the polytrap before monsters do.

Another answer is: skip the level as soon as out-of-depth monsters
appear.

You can, of course, make trap detection your first priority, if you
think this is wise. Detect traps (use orbs or confused gold detection,
etc.) as soon as you reach any level (starting from level 8), then
teleport adjacent to the trap and do what I suggested upthread. This
certainly requires some equipment that you may not have. (And I would
not suggest that procedere anyway.)

There are always many choices in Nethack; what's best depends on your
current game and the specific situation. There's no general solution
for everything.

